उद्-अव-√ सो P. -अ॑व-स्यति, to leave off, go away;
to finish, end, AV. ix, 6, 54; AitBr.; ŚBr.;
to go away to (another place, with loc.), ĀśvGṛ. iv, 1, 1.

उद्-√ 1. अश् P. -अश्नोति, (Subj. -अश्नवत्, RV. v, 59, 4; pf. -आनंश, RV. viii, 24, 12; aor. -आ॑नट् and -आनट्, &c.) Ā. (3. du. -अश्नुवाते, ŚBr. iv, 2, 1, 26)
to reach, attain, arrive at, ŚBr.;
to reach, be equal;
to overtake, surpass;
to master, rule, RV.

उद्-√ 2. अस् P. -अस्यति, to cast or throw up;
to raise, erect, elevate, ŚBr.; MBh.;
to throw out, expel, ŚBr. ii, 6, 2, 16; KātyŚr.;
to throw (a weapon), Naiṣ.

उद्-√ आस् Ā. -आस्ते, to sit separate or away from, sit on one side or apart;
to abstain from participating in;
to take no interest in, be unconcerned about, be indifferent or passive, MBh.; BhP.; Śiś. &c.;
to pass by, omit, Sarvad.

उद्-आ-√ 1. कृ P. Ā. -करोति, -कुरुते, (impf. -आ॑कर्, RV. x, 67, 4) to expel, drive out;
to fetch out of RV.; ŚBr.; TS.;
to select, choose, AV. xii, 4, 41; ŚBr. iii, 3, 1, 14;
 (only Ā. Pāṇ. i, 3, 32) to prick, Kāś. on Pāṇ. i, 3, 32;
to revile, abuse, ib.

उद्-आ-√ यम् P. (Impv. -आ॑यच्छतु) to bring out, fetch out, get fetch out, get off, AV. v, 30, 15 :
Ā. (aor. 3. sg. -आयत du. -आयसाताम् pl. -आयसत) to show, exhibit, make known, Pāṇ. i, 2, 15;
 (but also aor. -आयंस्त, in the sense to bring out, get off, Kāś. on Pāṇ. i, 2, 15.)

उद्-आर—ता, f. or उद्-आर—त्व, n. nobleness, generousness, liberality;
 energy, Kathās.; Daś.; Sarvad. &c.;
 elegance of speech or expression, Vām.; Sāh.

उद्-आर—ता, f. or उद्-आर—त्व, n. nobleness, generousness, liberality;
 energy, Kathās.; Daś.; Sarvad. &c.;
 elegance of speech or expression, Vām.; Sāh.

उद्-आ-√ वह् P. -वहति, to lead away, carry or draw away, ŚBr.; MBh.;
to marry, MBh.; R.;
to extol, praise, W.

उद्-आ-√ वृत् Caus. -वर्तयति, to cause to go out, excrete, Suśr.;
to secrete;
to retain (see the next).

उद्-आ-√ हृ P. -आ॑-हरति, to set up, put up, ŚBr. i, 1, 1, 22;
to relate, declare, announce;
to quote, cite, illustrate;
to name, call, ŚBr.; Gobh.; ĀśvŚr.; Baudh.; MBh.; RPrāt. &c.:
Pass. -ह्रिय॑ते, to be set up or put up, TS. vi, 2, 9, 4.
